      "page_title": "Why Async Database Access",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 1. Definition",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The ==event loop== runs on **one** thread",
            "A blocking call (`psycopg2`, `sqlite3`, sync `redis-py`) freezes it",
            "Every other coroutine waits until that call returns",
            "An ==async driver== yields at network I/O instead"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "# sync driver: loop frozen",
            "rows = cur.fetchall()",
            "# async driver: loop keeps going",
            "rows = await conn.fetch(sql)"
          ],
          "note": "only await hands control back"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 2. Mechanism",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "Task A",
                "sub": "await conn.fetch()",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "Loop",
                "sub": "serves Task B, C…",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "Postgres",
                "sub": "works, replies",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "Task A",
                "sub": "resumes with rows",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Async gives more ==concurrency==, not a faster query",
            "A 200 ms query is **still** 200 ms",
            "The win: many requests wait on I/O together"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Driver",
            "1 query",
            "10 at once"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "sync",
              "200 ms",
              "~2000 ms"
            ],
            [
              "async",
              "200 ms",
              "__~200 ms__"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
