      "page_title": "asyncpg Connections and Pools",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 1. Definition: One Connection",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "conn = await asyncpg.connect(dsn)",
            "try:",
            "    n = await conn.fetchval(q)",
            "finally:",
            "    await conn.close()  # always"
          ],
          "note": "unclosed conn leaks a Postgres backend"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Method",
            "Returns",
            "e.g."
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`fetch()`",
              "list of ==Record==",
              "all rows"
            ],
            [
              "`fetchrow()`",
              "one Record or **None**",
              "by id"
            ],
            [
              "`fetchval()`",
              "single value",
              "count(*)"
            ],
            [
              "`execute()`",
              "status string",
              "'INSERT 0 1'"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 2. Mechanism: The Pool",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "pool = await asyncpg.create_pool(",
            "    dsn, min_size=10,",
            "    max_size=10)  # both default 10",
            "async with pool.acquire() as c:",
            "    rows = await c.fetch(q)"
          ],
          "note": "released back to pool on exit"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Shortcuts `pool.fetch()` / `pool.execute()`: acquire → run → release",
            "On release: ==RESET ALL==, UNLISTEN, open cursors closed",
            "`max_inactive_connection_lifetime=300` s closes {purple:idle} conns"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def init(c):  # per conn",
            "  await c.set_type_codec('jsonb',",
            "    encoder=json.dumps,",
            "    decoder=json.loads,",
            "    schema='pg_catalog')"
          ],
          "note": "pass via create_pool(dsn, init=init)"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 3. Example: Params & Records",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "r = await conn.fetchrow(",
            "  'SELECT * FROM users'",
            "  ' WHERE id=$1 AND org=$2',",
            "  uid, org)  # sent separately",
            "r['name'], r[0], dict(r)"
          ],
          "note": "$1, $2 — never %s or ?"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Placeholders are **positional** `$1, $2`, not `%s` / `?`",
            "Values travel ==separately== from SQL text → no injection",
            "Record access: `r['name']`, `r[0]`, `dict(r)`"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Postgres",
            "Python"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "uuid",
              "`uuid.UUID`"
            ],
            [
              "timestamptz",
              "`datetime`"
            ],
            [
              "numeric",
              "`Decimal`"
            ],
            [
              "int[]",
              "`list[int]`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Two concurrent awaits on one `conn` → **InterfaceError**",
            "`%s` or `?` placeholders → syntax error; use `$1`",
            "Forgetting `close()` → leaked server connections",
            "Row-by-row INSERT loops for bulk → use ==COPY=="
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "postgresql",
      "subtitle": "connect, query, pool"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Bulk Loads, COPY & Pool Lifecycle",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "await conn.executemany(",
            "  'INSERT INTO t VALUES($1,$2)',",
            "  rows)  # batched",
            "await conn.copy_records_to_table(",
            "  't', records=rows)  # COPY"
          ],
          "note": "COPY often 10x+ faster than INSERTs"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 4. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "await asyncio.gather(",
            "  conn.fetch(q1), conn.fetch(q2))",
            "# InterfaceError: another",
            "# operation is in progress"
          ],
          "note": "one conn = one query at a time"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Fix",
          "text": "Give each task its own conn: `pool.fetch()` or `pool.acquire()` per task, never a shared `conn`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 5. Bulk loads compared",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Method",
            "Round trips",
            "Speed"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`execute()` in a loop",
              "N",
              "slowest"
            ],
            [
              "`executemany()`",
              "batched",
              "faster"
            ],
            [
              "`copy_records_to_table()`",
              "one ==COPY==",
              "**10x+**"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Few rows or need `ON CONFLICT` → `executemany()`",
            "Thousands of rows into one table → ==COPY==",
            "Pass `columns=[...]` to COPY a subset of columns",
            "Wrap the load in `conn.transaction()`: all or nothing"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 6. Pool lifecycle",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def lifespan(app):",
            "  app.pool = await create_pool(",
            "    dsn, init=init)  # startup",
            "  yield",
            "  await app.pool.close()  # drain"
          ],
          "note": "one pool per process, not per request"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`pool.acquire(timeout=5)` fails fast instead of queueing forever",
            "`pool.close()` waits for conns to be ==released==",
            "`pool.terminate()` closes **immediately**, no waiting",
            "`command_timeout=` on the pool caps every query"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 7. Takeaways",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`try/finally` or `async with` so conns always return",
            "One query at a time **per** connection",
            "Positional `$1` params: values never touch the SQL",
            "Per-conn setup (codecs) goes in ==init=="
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Default choice",
          "text": "Reach for `pool.fetch()` first; use `acquire()` only when several queries must share a conn or a ==transaction==."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "postgresql",
      "subtitle": "connect, query, pool"
    },
