    {
      "page_title": "Transactions, Isolation Levels & SKIP LOCKED",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 1. Definition: the transaction block",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`async with conn.transaction():` → **COMMIT** on clean exit",
            "Exception inside → ==ROLLBACK==, then the error re-raises",
            "Nested `transaction()` → a ==SAVEPOINT==; only it rolls back",
            "Options: `isolation=`, `readonly=`, `deferrable=`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with conn.transaction():",
            "    await conn.execute(q1)",
            "    async with conn.transaction():",
            "        await conn.execute(q2)"
          ],
          "note": "inner block = SAVEPOINT, not new tx"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "tx = conn.transaction(",
            "    isolation='serializable',",
            "    readonly=True,",
            "    deferrable=True)",
            "async with tx:  # no writes",
            "    rows = await conn.fetch(q)"
          ],
          "note": "deferrable: waits for safe snapshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 2. Mechanism: what each level sees",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "**READ COMMITTED** (default): each ==statement== sees data committed before it began",
            "REPEATABLE READ: ==one snapshot== for the whole transaction",
            "SERIALIZABLE (SSI): blocks every anomaly, may fail with ==40001==",
            "READ UNCOMMITTED = READ COMMITTED in Postgres: **no** dirty reads"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 3. Comparison: anomalies allowed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
